.TH SCROLLBARS 1
.SH NAME
scrollbars \- a window onto something much bigger
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/scrollbars
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I ScrollBars
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/ScrollBars.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
A map of 2048 pixels square with 256 trees on it, seen through a window
a fraction of the size.  The program does not manage the scrolling: it
declares the range and the window manager draws the bars, handles the
dragging and hands back a position, which the drawing subtracts.  The
original's aside \- "Check bounds if you wish better performance" \- is
that it draws all 256 trees whether or not they are on screen, and so
does this.
.PP
.IR wm (1)
has no scroll bars to declare a range to, so the port draws its own along
the right and bottom edges and drags them itself.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B LMB
Drag a scroll bar
.TP
.B arrows
Scroll
.TP
.B "any other key"
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/scrollbars.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
